W44-AUDIT-5 Phase 3: 3-mode A/B/D bisect on codec_wiki e7 d=4 + 2 photo cells

Status: HONEST-STOP — Mode D default-flip RULED OUT
=====================================================

Date: 2026-05-24
Source: jxl-encoder commit (Phase 3 source ships as OPT-IN API only)
Bench TSV: w44_audit_5_phase3_mode_bisect_2026-05-24.tsv
Reproducer: jxl-encoder/examples/w44_audit_5_phase3_mode_bisect.rs

Modes compared
---------------
  Mode A  - Current Zenjxl baseline. LS warm-start CfL + LS-only refinement.
            Field: cfl_pass1_screenshot_x0_start = false (default).
  Mode B  - EncoderStrategy::Libjxl, bit-exact cjxl-parity. libjxl Newton
            (eps=100, max_iters=20, `x = 0` start, no LS fallback) ALWAYS,
            on EVERY image. Strict cjxl-parity byte-lock invariant holds.
  Mode D  - Zenjxl with cfl_pass1_screenshot_x0_start = true OPT-IN.
            Per-image content-class router: when ZenanalyzeProxies indicate
            `m3_colourfulness >= W44_AUDIT_6_HIGH_COLOUR_M3_MIN = 80.0`
            (i.e. mixed-content screenshots like codec_wiki), the CfL
            Pass-1 + Pass-2 SIMD calls flip `libjxl_parity = true` for
            that single image only. Photos (M3 < 40 on CID22) stay on
            the LS warm-start path.

